# Vendored upstream manifests are integrity-pinned: their sha256 is recorded in
# the CNI and addon definitions and verified against the bytes on disk, so a
# swapped or corrupted manifest fails a test rather than a live cluster.
#
# Git must therefore never rewrite these bytes. Without `-text`, autocrlf
# converts them to CRLF on Windows checkout and every digest check fails
# locally while passing on Linux CI -- which trains people to ignore a
# supply-chain integrity failure.
backend/api/data/** -text
